Subject: boot-class modules from the first sysinit entry (U15)

S3-B5 (2026-10-26): the first boot-class load panicked in process 0.
rth1_mountroot calls dlm_marc_post with interrupts masked (psw 0x2700),
and lf_hashload's vn_rdwr faulted (bus error) on a page the file system
maps for the read, which cannot be brought in there.  That answers U15
the way 30 section 3 provided for: the load moves to the first sysinit
entry.  modadm MOD_C_POST runs it once a boot from a process (modadmin
-B); dlm_marc_post loads nothing while interrupts are masked and says
where the modules load.  The harness checks MOD_C_POST and its once.

